an notice different details without inventing them.\n\nHowever, a sensible explanation is not automatically a reliable one. Dates, maps and other records should be used to check the accounts. A preliminary comparison can reveal questions that deserve further investigation. If a writer could not predict a later event, a detailed description of that event may suggest that the account was revised afterward. This is a possible clue, not proof by itself.\n\nThe historian then examines a larger range of sources. Each has strengths and limitations, and a cautious revision of the first interpretation may be needed. Understanding a journey requires more than selecting the most entertaining story: it requires asking who wrote each account, for whom, when, and for what purpose."},{"n":99,"id":"v99","word":"range","text":"In \"Reading a Journey Through Different Eyes\", <u>range</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["physical condition of a document","variety or extent","exact date of completion","degree of personal agreement"],"key":1,"explanation":"The historian consults a wider variety of sources.","source":"Shared travel reading and vocabulary theme","passageTitle":"Reading a Journey Through Different Eyes","passage":"Consider a historian who plans to undertake a study of an old journey. Two travelers left accounts of the same route, but one describes business arrangements while the other records daily life. Each account offers a unique contribution: something not provided in quite the same way by the other. Neither should automatically be treated as a complete record.\n\nThe travelers may describe the same vehicle differently. A passenger interested in comfort might discuss the seats, while a merchant concentrates on the space for goods. Their purposes help explain which features receive emphasis. A historian should not presume that every difference is an error; people can notice different details without inventing them.\n\nHowever, a sensible explanation is not automatically a reliable one. Dates, maps and other records should be used to check the accounts. A preliminary comparison can reveal questions that deserve further investigation. If a writer could not predict a later event, a detailed description of that event may suggest that the account was revised afterward. This is a possible clue, not proof by itself.\n\nThe historian then examines a larger range of sources. Each has strengths and limitations, and a cautious revision of the first interpretation may be needed. Understanding a journey requires more than selecting the most entertaining story: it requires asking who wrote each account, for whom, when, and for what purpose."},{"n":100,"id":"v100","word":"revision","text":"In \"Reading a Journey Through Different Eyes\", <u>revision</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["repetition without any alteration","summary copied from another writer","change made after reconsideration","division into equal sections"],"key":2,"explanation":"New evidence may require the historian to change the first interpretation.","source":"Shared vocabulary and reading material","passageTitle":"Reading a Journey Through Different Eyes","passage":"Consider a historian who plans to undertake a study of an old journey. Two travelers left accounts of the same route, but one describes business arrangements while the other records daily life. Each account offers a unique contribution: something not provided in quite the same way by the other. Neither should automatically be treated as a complete record.\n\nThe travelers may describe the same vehicle differently. A passenger interested in comfort might discuss the seats, while a merchant concentrates on the space for goods. Their purposes help explain which features receive emphasis. A historian should not presume that every difference is an error; people can notice different details without inventing them.\n\nHowever, a sensible explanation is not automatically a reliable one. Dates, maps and other records should be used to check the accounts. A preliminary comparison can reveal questions that deserve further investigation. If a writer could not predict a later event, a detailed description of that event may suggest that the account was revised afterward. This is a possible clue, not proof by itself.\n\nThe historian then examines a larger range of sources. Each has strengths and limitations, and a cautious revision of the first interpretation may be needed. Understanding a journey requires more than selecting the most entertaining story: it requires asking who wrote each account, for whom, when, and for what purpose."}]'::jsonb; expected jsonb := '[{"n":1,"text":"In Passage 1, <u>abandon</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["give up","look into","repair","set up"],"key":0,"explanation":"The college chose not to give up its plan for the courtyard.","id":"v1"},{"n":2,"text":"In Passage 1, <u>acquire</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["forget","describe","display","gain"],"key":3,"explanation":"Students would gain skills through practical gardening.","id":"v2"},{"n":3,"text":"In Passage 1, <u>accurate</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["correct and exact","recently discovered","easy to carry","quickly drawn"],"key":0,"explanation":"Checking each measurement makes the map exact.","id":"v3"},{"n":4,"text":"In Passage 1, <u>adjacent</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["different from","far beyond","next to","hidden beneath"],"key":2,"explanation":"The library is in the building next to the courtyard.","id":"v4"},{"n":5,"text":"In Passage 1, <u>allocate</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["set aside for a purpose","calculate incorrectly","remove completely","collect from visitors"],"key":0,"explanation":"Staff assigned part of an existing budget to tools.","id":"v5"},{"n":6,"text":"In Passage 1, <u>anticipate</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["cause immediately","expect in advance","measure precisely","ignore entirely"],"key":1,"explanation":"Students expected a future water shortage and planned for it.","id":"v6"},{"n":7,"text":"In Passage 1, <u>detect</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["prevent every occurrence of","increase the size of","discover the presence of","make a record of"],"key":2,"explanation":"Inspections helped students find leaks that were already present.","id":"v7"},{"n":8,"text":"In Passage 1, <u>distinct</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["closely connected","clearly different","temporarily closed","equally expensive"],"key":1,"explanation":"The courtyard areas have different, clearly separated purposes.","id":"v8"},{"n":9,"text":"In Passage 1, <u>document</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["delay","record","advertise","question"],"key":1,"explanation":"Photographs and written notes provide a record of changes.","id":"v9"},{"n":10,"text":"In Passage 1, <u>establish</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["take part in","pay a fee to","move away from","set up"],"key":3,"explanation":"They aimed to start a club that would continue into the future.","id":"v10"},{"n":11,"text":"In Passage 2, <u>empirical</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["designed for profit","based on tradition","based on observation","impossible to repeat"],"key":2,"explanation":"The team collected observations instead of relying on opinions.","id":"v11"},{"n":12,"text":"In Passage 2, <u>environment</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["personal ability","final decision","required equipment","surrounding conditions"],"key":3,"explanation":"The study environment includes the conditions in each room.","id":"v12"},{"n":13,"text":"In Passage 2, <u>evaluate</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["decorate","assess","combine","reserve"],"key":1,"explanation":"The team used a task to assess each study room.","id":"v13"},{"n":14,"text":"In Passage 2, <u>exceed</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["depend on","fall below","remain near","go above"],"key":3,"explanation":"The noise could not go above the stated limit.","id":"v14"},{"n":15,"text":"In Passage 2, <u>external</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["heard only by researchers","made by machines","coming from outside","continuing without a break"],"key":2,"explanation":"Road noise came from outside the study rooms.","id":"v15"},{"n":16,"text":"In Passage 2, <u>facilitate</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["make easier","carry out alone","explain afterward","make compulsory"],"key":0,"explanation":"Clear instructions would make the task easier to understand.","id":"v16"},{"n":17,"text":"In Passage 2, <u>fluctuate</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["remain unchanged","rise and fall","become identical","improve permanently"],"key":1,"explanation":"Scores could move up and down on different days.","id":"v17"},{"n":18,"text":"In Passage 2, <u>hypothesis</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["equipment used for measurement","proposed explanation to be tested","rule already enforced","conclusion that cannot change"],"key":1,"explanation":"The team was testing an explanation about predictable sounds.","id":"v18"},{"n":19,"text":"In Passage 2, <u>minor</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["difficult to measure","similar in every way","small in importance or size","caused deliberately"],"key":2,"explanation":"The differences were small, although further monitoring was needed.","id":"v19"},{"n":20,"text":"In Passage 2, <u>monitor</u> is closest in meaning to:","options":["compare only once","bring to an end","track over time","make public immediately"],"key":2,"explanation":"The team kept checking performance for several weeks.","id":"v20"},{"n":21,"text":"The redesigned classroom can <u>accommodate</u> forty students without becoming crowded.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["charge a fee to","hold comfortably","replace permanently","teach independently"],"key":1,"explanation":"The room has enough comfortable space for forty students.","id":"v21"},{"n":22,"text":"The report <u>acknowledges</u> that its conclusions are based on a limited sample.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["conceals","denies","predicts","admits"],"key":3,"explanation":"The report openly accepts this limitation.","id":"v22"},{"n":23,"text":"Some plants can <u>adapt</u> to a drier climate over many generations.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["escape","return","contribute","adjust"],"key":3,"explanation":"They become suited to changed environmental conditions.","id":"v23"},{"n":24,"text":"The evidence is <u>adequate</u> to support a small pilot study, but not a national policy.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["sufficient","confidential","unusual","unnecessary"],"key":0,"explanation":"There is enough evidence for the limited purpose stated.","id":"v24"},{"n":25,"text":"Several teachers <u>advocate</u> giving students feedback before they receive a final grade.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["support","express surprise at","require payment for","postpone"],"key":0,"explanation":"The teachers argue in favor of this approach.","id":"v25"},{"n":26,"text":"Because the instructions were <u>ambiguous</u>, two groups interpreted them differently.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["unusually strict","written in a foreign language","easy to remember","open to more than one meaning"],"key":3,"explanation":"Different reasonable interpretations indicate unclear meaning.","id":"v26"},{"n":27,"text":"The lecturer used an <u>analogy</u> between a city transport network and blood circulation.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["disagreement","experiment","comparison","historical account"],"key":2,"explanation":"Two different systems are compared to explain an idea.","id":"v27"},{"n":28,"text":"The society holds its <u>annual</u> exhibition every November.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["yearly","weekly","permanent","unexpected"],"key":0,"explanation":"An annual event takes place once each year.","id":"v28"},{"n":29,"text":"Researchers <u>derive</u> information about ancient climates from layers of ice.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["hide","protect","obtain","remove completely"],"key":2,"explanation":"They obtain information by studying ice layers.","id":"v29"},{"n":30,"text":"The benefits of extra practice <u>diminish</u> when students are too tired to concentrate.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["appear suddenly","remain equal","spread widely","become smaller"],"key":3,"explanation":"Tired students gain less benefit from additional practice.","id":"v30"},{"n":31,"text":"Volunteers will <u>distribute</u> reusable bottles to everyone at the event.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["describe","give out","manufacture","collect back"],"key":1,"explanation":"The bottles will be handed out to participants.","id":"v31"},{"n":32,"text":"The project brought together a <u>diverse</u> group of students from many backgrounds.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["newly qualified","closely related","varied","highly experienced"],"key":2,"explanation":"Many backgrounds make the group varied.","id":"v32"},{"n":33,"text":"The new filter will <u>eliminate</u> most of the dust from the air entering the room.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["produce","measure","identify","remove"],"key":3,"explanation":"The filter takes most dust out of the incoming air.","id":"v33"},{"n":34,"text":"A small grant will <u>enable</u> the team to buy the equipment it needs.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["make it possible for","make it unnecessary for","remind","force"],"key":0,"explanation":"The grant provides the means to make the purchase.","id":"v34"},{"n":35,"text":"Adding clear examples can <u>enhance</u> the quality of an explanation.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["improve","test","replace","restrict"],"key":0,"explanation":"Examples can make the explanation better.","id":"v35"},{"n":36,"text":"The two courses require an <u>equivalent</u> amount of independent study.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["increasing","equal","limited","unknown"],"key":1,"explanation":"Both courses require the same amount of study.","id":"v36"},{"n":37,"text":"Because the available funding is <u>finite</u>, not every proposal can be supported.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["reliable","shared","flexible","limited"],"key":3,"explanation":"There is a fixed limit to the money available.","id":"v37"},{"n":38,"text":"The policy provides a <u>framework</u> within which individual teachers can plan lessons.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["basic structure","detailed transcript","final examination","financial reward"],"key":0,"explanation":"The policy supplies an organizing structure, not every lesson detail.","id":"v38"},{"n":39,"text":"The revised course will <u>incorporate</u> more practical work alongside lectures.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["replace","include","evaluate","postpone"],"key":1,"explanation":"Practical work becomes part of the course.","id":"v39"},{"n":40,"text":"Some delay was <u>inevitable</u> because every road to the village was flooded.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["unavoidable","unexpected","unimportant","brief"],"key":0,"explanation":"With every road blocked, delay could not be avoided.","id":"v40"},{"n":41,"text":"An <u>objective</u> assessment should depend on evidence rather than the examiner''s personal preferences.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["rapid","favorable","detailed","impartial"],"key":3,"explanation":"An impartial assessment is not biased by personal preference.","id":"v41"},{"n":42,"text":"Lower printing costs helped <u>offset</u> the increase in the price of paper.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["explain","compensate for","predict","add to"],"key":1,"explanation":"Savings in one area counterbalanced an increase in another.","id":"v42"},{"n":43,"text":"Water temperature was the only <u>parameter</u> changed between the two experiments.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["unexpected error","final result","measurable condition","scientific instrument"],"key":2,"explanation":"Temperature was the experimental condition deliberately varied.","id":"v43"},{"n":44,"text":"If the symptoms <u>persist</u> after several days, the patient should seek further advice.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["continue","change location","improve","appear suddenly"],"key":0,"explanation":"Persistent symptoms continue rather than disappear.","id":"v44"},{"n":45,"text":"The interviews offered a different <u>perspective</u> on the neighborhood redevelopment plan.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["set of instructions","point of view","period of time","source of funding"],"key":1,"explanation":"The interviews revealed another way of viewing the plan.","id":"v45"},{"n":46,"text":"Laboratory rules <u>prohibit</u> eating near the research equipment.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["forbid","recommend","require","supervise"],"key":0,"explanation":"The rules do not allow eating in that area.","id":"v46"},{"n":47,"text":"The course in <u>psychology</u> examines how people learn, remember, and make decisions.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["the study of ancient languages","the study of rock formation","the study of mind and behavior","the study of weather patterns"],"key":2,"explanation":"Learning, memory, and decisions are topics within psychology.","id":"v47"},{"n":48,"text":"The coordinator helped the two clubs <u>resolve</u> their disagreement about the room.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["repeat","settle","investigate","report"],"key":1,"explanation":"The clubs reached a solution to their disagreement.","id":"v48"},{"n":49,"text":"The town needs a reliable water supply to <u>sustain</u> its community gardens.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["expand","inspect","advertise","maintain"],"key":3,"explanation":"A dependable water supply keeps the gardens functioning.","id":"v49"},{"n":50,"text":"The survey found <u>widespread</u> support for safer walking routes throughout the city.<br>Choose the closest meaning of the underlined word.","options":["limited to one group","recently withdrawn","existing across many places","expressed very strongly"],"key":2,"explanation":"Support across the city is broadly distributed.","id":"v50"}]'::jsonb;
begin
select * into strict c from public.monthly_ai_catalog where exam_id='ibt-november-2026' for update;
if c.version='2026-11-25-vocabulary-100-v3' then return;end if;
if c.version<>'2026-11-24-speaking-v2' or c.content->>'version'<>'2026-11-24-speaking-v2' then raise exception 'Unexpected current iBT revision; no update applied';end if;
if (select jsonb_array_length(s->'questions') from jsonb_array_elements(c.content->'objective') s where s->>'id'='vocabulary')<>50 then raise exception 'Expected the earlier 50-question vocabulary catalogue';end if;
if exists(select 1 from jsonb_array_elements(c.content->'objective') s cross join lateral jsonb_array_elements(s->'questions') with ordinality a(q,ord) where s->>'id'='vocabulary' and (q->'id' is distinct from (expected->((ord-1)::int))->'id' or q->'key' is distinct from (expected->((ord-1)::int))->'key' or q->'options' is distinct from (expected->((ord-1)::int))->'options')) then raise exception 'The earlier answer key does not match the student page; no update applied';end if;
select jsonb_agg(case when s->>'id'='vocabulary' then jsonb_set(s,'{questions}',(s->'questions')||extra) else s end order by ord) into objective from jsonb_array_elements(c.content->'objective') with ordinality a(s,ord);
update public.monthly_ai_catalog set version='2026-11-25-vocabulary-100-v3',content=jsonb_set(c.content,'{objective}',objective)||jsonb_build_object('version','2026-11-25-vocabulary-100-v3','_history',coalesce(c.content->'_history','{}'::jsonb)||jsonb_build_object(c.version,c.content-'_history'-'_legacyVersion')) where exam_id=c.exam_id;
end $vocabulary$;
commit;
select c.exam_id,c.version,(select jsonb_array_length(s->'questions') from jsonb_array_elements(c.content->'objective') s where s->>'id'='vocabulary') as vocabulary_questions,c.content->>'_legacyVersion' as legacy_version,jsonb_object_keys(c.content->'_history') as archived_version from public.monthly_ai_catalog c where exam_id='ibt-november-2026';
